.8,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":null,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":null,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.16905924222761637,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.00495768828224552,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":27.5,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.09131845798664673,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.004219559849932941,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":55.3,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.01509,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":10.1,"_gate_insider_buying":0.444,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":44.4,"pf":[],"description_full":"Bread Financial Holdings, Inc. provides tech-forward payment and lending solutions to customers and consumer-based industries in North America. It offers credit card and other loans financing services, including risk management solutions, underwriting, and funding services for private label and co-brand credit card programs, as well as through Bread Pay partnerships. The company also manages and services the loans it originates for private label, co-brand, and general-purpose credit card programs, and installment loans and split-pay products; and provides marketing, and data and analytics services. In addition, it offers an enhanced digital suite that includes a unified software development kit, which provides access to its suite of products, as well as promotes credit payment options earlier in the shopping experience. Further, the company through Bread Pay, a digital payments platform and robust suite of application programming interfaces allows merchants and partners to integrate online point-of-sale financing and other digital payment products. Additionally, it offers retail and deposit products, primarily in the form of certificates of deposit and high-yield savings accounts, including traditional and Roth Individual Retirement Accounts. The company offers its products under the Bread, Bread Financial, Bread Cashback, Bread Rewards, Bread Pay, and Bread Savings brands. The company was formerly known as Alliance Data Systems Corporation and changed its name to Bread Financial Holdings, Inc. in March 2022. Bread Financial Holdings, Inc. was incorporated in 1995 and is headquartered in Columbus, Ohio.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Ralph J. Andretta | President, CEO & Director | Age 64 | Compensation: $4.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 6K people. Stock-based compensation of $9K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Bread Financial Holdings, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $3.9B market cap.","The top line has compounded at -12% over the past three years and +0% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 9.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.3M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2323281.6},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 20% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Financial Survey: Consumer Portfolio Services (NASDAQ:CPSS) vs. Bread Financial (NYSE:BFH)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/financial-survey-consumer-portfolio-services-nasdaqcpss-vs-bread-financial-nysebfh.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793986136.0,"origin"